WEBVTT

1
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:02,580
Cut the crow sister

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:05,180
Why don't I trade the mask for a whole piece of meat, just this once?

3
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:06,380
I'll figure it out tomorrow

4
00:00:11,370 --> 00:00:12,370
One pack for one rabbit

5
00:00:12,370 --> 00:00:14,370
Sister Pei Ya said there should be at least two, so forget it.

6
00:00:14,370 --> 00:00:15,570
Just one. Just one.

7
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:16,970
Replacing a pack of facial masks is too expensive

8
00:00:16,970 --> 00:00:17,970
You are short of meat now

9
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:19,370
We have no shortage of facial masks and we have to change them.

10
00:00:19,370 --> 00:00:20,970
That half is okay

11
00:00:20,970 --> 00:00:25,700
Half a rabbit for a pack, both parties can exchange it voluntarily

12
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:27,740
You pay for a facial mask

13
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:29,140
You can have someone do a day's work for you

14
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:31,340
Now only half of the whole pack is exchanged

15
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:37,760
Stop talking nonsense and bring me your stuff, Sister Fei

16
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:38,960
You still have salt

17
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:40,560
Changed from the last overworked job

18
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:41,560
Not willing to use it all at once

19
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:44,100
You are too counter-intuitive.

20
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,500
Not a good thing either

21
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:46,500
It's salt

22
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:47,520
I dare

23
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:48,720
The car is not a god

24
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:51,120
He can roast peaches, boil salt, and fish.

25
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:52,520
Why can't we learn if we just do it?

26
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:53,520
Wait until we have a plenary session

27
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:55,320
Let's see what else he can show off in front of us

28
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:57,150
Then before making the salt tomorrow

29
00:00:57,150 --> 00:00:58,550
Can you calculate the number of firewood pots first?

30
00:00:58,550 --> 00:01:00,150
Too much was burned last time

31
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:01,550
We almost ran out of fire at night

32
00:01:01,950 --> 00:01:04,380
Tomorrow I'll bring the salt as you asked

33
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:06,310
I will definitely make it
